<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Autom Methods Manag Chem</journal-id><journal-title>Journal of Automated Methods &#x00026; Management in Chemistry</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1463-9246</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1464-5068</issn></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">17671620</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">1903454</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="pii">S1463924606513422</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/JAMMC/2006/51342</article-id>	<article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Direct Determination of Moisture in Powder Milk Using Near Infrared Spectroscopy</article-title></title-group><contrib-group>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Nagarajan</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><address><email>rajan.npl@gmail.com</email></address><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>Parul</given-names></name><address><email>parul@mail.nplindia.ernet.in</email></address><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>					<contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Mehrotra</surname><given-names>Ranjana</given-names></name><address><email>ranjana@mail.nplindia.ernet.in</email></address><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>					</contrib-group>						<aff id="aff1"><label>1</label>				<addr-line>Optical Radiation Standards</addr-line>				<addr-line>National Physical Laboratory</addr-line>				<addr-line>K. S. Krishnan Road</addr-line>				<addr-line>New Delhi</addr-line>				<addr-line>110012</addr-line>				<country>India</country>			</aff>			<pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>2006</year></pub-date><volume>2006</volume><elocation-id>51342</elocation-id><history><date date-type="received"><day>24</day><month>1</month><year>2006</year></date><date date-type="rev-recd"><day>6</day><month>3</month><year>2006</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>18</day><month>5</month><year>2006</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2006 R.  Nagarajan et al.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2006</copyright-year><copyright-holder>R. Nagarajan, Parul Singh, Ranjana Mehrotra</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract>		<p>Moisture content in commercially available milk powder was investigated using near infrared (NIR) diffuse reflectance spectroscopy with an Indian low-cost dispersive NIR spectrophotometer. Different packets of milk powder of the same batch were procured from the market. Forty-five samples with moisture range 4&#x02013;10% were prepared in the laboratory. Spectra of the samples were collected in the wavelength region 800&#x02013;2500 nm. Moisture values of all the samples were simultaneously determined by Karl Fischer (KF) titration. These KF values were used as reference for developing calibration model using partial least squares regression (PLSR) method. The calibration and validation statistics are <inline-formula><mml:math id="M1" overflow="scroll" display="inline">  <mml:msubsup>   <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>   <mml:mrow><mml:mtext>&#x02009;</mml:mtext>    <mml:mi>c</mml:mi><mml:mi>a</mml:mi><mml:mi>l</mml:mi>   </mml:mrow>   <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>  </mml:msubsup>  <mml:mo>:</mml:mo><mml:mn>0.9942</mml:mn></mml:math></inline-formula>, <inline-formula><mml:math id="M2" overflow="scroll" display="inline">  <mml:mtext>RMSEC</mml:mtext><mml:mo>:</mml:mo><mml:mn>0.1040</mml:mn></mml:math></inline-formula>, and <inline-formula><mml:math id="M3" overflow="scroll" display="inline">  <mml:msubsup>   <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>   <mml:mrow><mml:mtext>&#x02009;</mml:mtext>    <mml:mi>v</mml:mi><mml:mi>a</mml:mi><mml:mi>l</mml:mi>   </mml:mrow>   <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>  </mml:msubsup>  <mml:mo>:</mml:mo><mml:mn>0.9822</mml:mn></mml:math></inline-formula>,<inline-formula><mml:math id="M4" overflow="scroll" display="inline">  <mml:mtext>RMSEV</mml:mtext><mml:mo>:</mml:mo><mml:mn>0.1730</mml:mn></mml:math></inline-formula>. Five samples of unknown moisture contentswere taken for NIR prediction using developed calibration model.The agreement between NIR predicted results and those of KarlFischer values is appreciable. The result shows that theinstrument can be successfully used for the determination ofmoisture content in milk powder.</p>	</abstract></article-meta></front></article>